-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA), 07-a0-00, Part 7 Division 3 (Transitional provisions relating to
-- the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024): ss 99 and 100 (inserted by that Act s 55, in operation
-- 16 May 2024), and s 30 as in force before 29 July 2024, which s 99 continues for some agreements.
-- Source: sources/rta-1987.07-a0-00.mrdoc_49316.txt lines 2479-2495; the former text of s 30 is the
-- present text with the two changes the 2024 Act s 25 made (sources/rtaa-2024.as-passed.mrdoc_47004.txt
-- lines 319-324: "a form approved by the Minister" became "the approved form" and "6 months" became
-- "12 months"), as s 30 stood after the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2011 s 27 (1 July 2013,
-- sources/rtaa-2011.as-passed.mrdoc_23067.txt lines 1464-1483); r 5CA modifies its s 30(2)(a) for fixed
-- terms entered into before 1 July 2013. Reference register REF-39, REF-40 (encoded), REF-41 (fact).
-- "commencement" in ss 99 and 100: the day the 2024 Act s 25 came into operation, 29 July 2024
-- (SL 2024/143 cl. 2(f)). LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`
IMPORT `regulations-1989`
IMPORT `part-6-boundary`
IMPORT `part-5-termination`
IMPORT `part-4-div-1-rent-and-bonds`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-act-extra`

§ `The commencement`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 99(1), 100(1) "commencement"; SL 2024/143 cl. 2(f); reference register REF-41
`the commencement` MEANS `day number` 2024 7 29

§ `Section 30 as in force before the commencement`

-- Former s 30(1): "... by written notice to the tenant, in a form approved by the Minister, ...". FK-26,
-- reading taken (A): a notice in the form approved under s 88C is not invalidated if its deviations from
-- the Minister's form are immaterial and not misleading (Interpretation Act s 74).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 30(1) as in force before 29 July 2024; Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) s 74; fork FK-26 reading A
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `former s 30(1) -- the notice has the form the subsection required` n IF
        n's `given by the lessor`
    AND n's `in writing`
    AND (   (n's `form` EQUALS `a form approved by the Minister`)
         OR (    (n's `form` EQUALS `the approved form (s 88C)`)
             AND `s 74 -- the form used is not invalidated, its deviations being immaterial and not misleading:` (n's `any departure from the required form is immaterial and not misleading`)))
    AND n's `specifies the increased rent or the change`
    AND n's `specifies the day`

-- Former s 30(1)(b): "not less than 6 months after the day on which the tenancy commenced, or, if the rent
-- has been increased under this section, the day on which it was last so increased". The day the months
-- run from is worked out as for the present s 30(1)(b) (part-4), under the same readings.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 30(1)(b) as in force before 29 July 2024; Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) ss 61(1)(b), 62
GIVEN k        IS A `Reading of s 30(1)(b)`
      n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` k `, former s 30(1)(b) -- the day of` n `under` a `is not less than 6 months after the day the months run from, given` h `and the holidays` holidays IF
    IF k EQUALS `FK-15 reading B`
    THEN e GREATER THAN `the last day of the period of` 6 `months after day` r
    ELSE e AT LEAST `the last day of the period of` 6 `months after day` r
    WHERE
        e MEANS n's `takes effect on`
        r MEANS `on` k `, s 30(1)(b) -- the day the 12 months run from, for an increase on day` e `under` a `, given` h `and the holidays` holidays

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 30 as in force before 29 July 2024; Residential Tenancies Regulations 1989 (WA) rr 5B, 5CA
GIVEN k        IS A `Reading of s 30(1)(b)`
      n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` k `, former s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays IF
        `s 30(1) -- the subsection applies to` a
    AND `former s 30(1) -- the notice has the form the subsection required` n
    AND "(a)" ... `s 30(1)(a) -- the day is not less than 60 days after the notice is given` n
    AND "(b)" ... `on` k `, former s 30(1)(b) -- the day of` n `under` a `is not less than 6 months after the day the months run from, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
    AND "(2)(a)" ... `s 30(2)(a) -- the right to increase is exercisable for` n `under` a `, given the holidays` holidays
    AND "(2)(b)" ... `s 30(2)(b) -- the right is not excluded and the increase is within any agreed limit, for` n `under` a
    AND "(3)" ... NOT n's `withdrawn`

§ `Section 99 -- Variation of rent for fixed term residential tenancy agreement entered, renewed or extended before commencement`

-- The facts ss 99 and 100 read about an agreement. `the current term ends on`: s 99(2)(b), "the original,
-- renewed or extended term of the agreement (the current term), disregarding any further renewal or
-- extension of the agreement".
DECLARE `Facts for sections 99 and 100` HAS
    `entered into, or last renewed or extended, before the commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the current term ends on`                                           IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `in force on the commencement`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts as the agreement record gives them, where it was not renewed or extended: entered into before
-- 29 July 2024, its current term ending on its expiry day, in force on 29 July 2024 if its tenancy had
-- commenced by then and it had not terminated before then. No provision beyond ss 99-100.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 99(2), 100(2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
GIVETH A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
`the facts for ss 99 and 100 of` a MEANS
    `Facts for sections 99 and 100` WITH
        `entered into, or last renewed or extended, before the commencement` IS (a's `entered into on` LESS THAN `the commencement`)
        `the current term ends on`                                           IS `s 3 -- the expiry day of` a
        `in force on the commencement`                                       IS (`s 3 -- day` `the commencement` `falls in the tenancy period of` a)

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 99(2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 99(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f IF
        "a residential tenancy agreement that creates a tenancy for a fixed term" ... a's `kind` EQUALS `a tenancy for a fixed term`
    AND "(a) entered into, or last renewed or extended, before the commencement" ... f's `entered into, or last renewed or extended, before the commencement`
    AND "(b) the current term ... ends after the commencement"
    ... (CONSIDER f's `the current term ends on`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST t THEN t GREATER THAN `the commencement`)

§ `Section 100 -- Variation of rent for residential tenancy agreement, other than fixed term agreement, entered before commencement`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 100(2)
GIVEN a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`, f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 100(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f IF
        "a residential tenancy agreement in force on the commencement" ... f's `in force on the commencement`
    AND "other than an agreement to which section 99 applies" ... NOT `s 99(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f

§ `Which version of section 30 governs an increase`

DECLARE `Version of section 30` IS ONE OF
    `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
    `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024`

-- s 99(3): "Section 30, as in force from time to time before the commencement, continues to apply to the
-- residential tenancy agreement until the end of the current term as if the Residential Tenancies Amendment
-- Act 2024 had not been enacted." s 100(3): ss 30 and 31A as in force from the commencement apply to the
-- other agreements in force on the commencement. FK-22, reading taken (A): the version that governs an
-- increase is the one that applies to the agreement on the day the increase is to take effect. An
-- increase that took effect before 29 July 2024 was governed by the former version (subject to s 100(4),
-- FK-21).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 99(3), 100(3); fork FK-22 reading A
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A `Version of section 30`
`the version of s 30 that governs` n `under` a `, given` f MEANS
    IF `s 99(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f
    THEN CONSIDER f's `the current term ends on`
         WHEN JUST t THEN IF n's `takes effect on` AT MOST t THEN `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024` ELSE `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
    ELSE IF n's `takes effect on` LESS THAN `the commencement`
         THEN `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024`
         ELSE `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`

-- FK-22, reading rejected (B): the version is fixed by the day the notice is given: under a s 99 agreement,
-- a notice given before the end of the current term is governed by the former version even if the increase
-- is to take effect after that term ends.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 99(3); fork FK-22 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A `Version of section 30`
`FK-22 reading B -- the version of s 30 that governs` n `under` a `, given` f MEANS
    IF `s 99(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f
    THEN CONSIDER f's `the current term ends on`
         WHEN JUST t THEN
             CONSIDER `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (n's `given`)
             WHEN JUST g THEN IF g AT MOST t THEN `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024` ELSE `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024`
    ELSE `the version of s 30 that governs` n `under` a `, given` f

§ `Section 100(4) -- notices given before the commencement`

-- s 100(4): "A notice of increase of rent relating to the residential tenancy agreement given under section
-- 30 or 31A before the commencement has no effect if the notice does not comply with that section as in
-- force from the commencement." FK-21, reading taken (A): it reaches a notice whose increase is to take
-- effect on or after the commencement; an increase that took effect before then was duly done under the
-- former s 30 and the deletion of "6 months" does not affect it (Interpretation Act ss 5 "repeal",
-- 37(1)(b); the explanatory memorandum for Bill 140 reads it the same way).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 100(4); Interpretation Act 1984 (WA) ss 5, 37(1)(b); fork FK-21 reading A
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 100(4) -- reaches the notice` n `under` a `, given` f IF
        `s 100(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f
    AND (CONSIDER `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (n's `given`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST g THEN g LESS THAN `the commencement`)
    AND NOT `s 37(1)(b) -- the repeal leaves the thing unaffected, it having been duly done before:` (n's `takes effect on` LESS THAN `the commencement`) `, a contrary intention appearing:` FALSE

-- FK-21, reading rejected (B): s 100(4) reaches every notice given before the commencement, including one
-- whose increase took effect before it (s 100(4) being the contrary intention s 37 allows for).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 100(4); fork FK-21 reading B
GIVEN n IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      f IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-21 reading B -- s 100(4) -- reaches the notice` n `under` a `, given` f IF
        `s 100(2) -- the section applies to` a `, given` f
    AND (CONSIDER `s 85 -- the day the notice is given` (n's `given`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
         WHEN JUST g THEN g LESS THAN `the commencement`)

§ `The notice of increase, under whichever version governs it`

-- Whether a notice of increase of rent increases the rent from the day it specifies, applying s 100(4) to
-- a notice it reaches (the notice then has effect only if it complies with the present s 30 or s 31A),
-- and otherwise the version of s 30 that governs it (s 99(3), s 100(3)), or the present s 31A.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30, 31A, 99, 100
GIVEN k        IS A `Reading of s 30(1)(b)`
      n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      f        IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on` k `, the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays IF
    IF (n's `under` EQUALS `section 31A`) OR (n's `under` EQUALS `section 31A as in force before 29 July 2024`)
    THEN `s 31A -- the notice` n `changes the method under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
    ELSE IF `s 100(4) -- reaches the notice` n `under` a `, given` f
         THEN `on` k `, s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
         ELSE CONSIDER `the version of s 30 that governs` n `under` a `, given` f
              WHEN `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024` THEN `on` k `, former s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
              WHEN `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024` THEN `on` k `, s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30, 31A, 99, 100
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      f        IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays IF
    `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays

-- The same, with s 100(4) on FK-21 reading B.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30, 99, 100; fork FK-21 reading B
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      f        IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-21 reading B -- the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays IF
    IF `FK-21 reading B -- s 100(4) -- reaches the notice` n `under` a `, given` f
    THEN `s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
    ELSE `the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays

-- The same, with the version chosen on FK-22 reading B.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) ss 30, 99; fork FK-22 reading B
GIVEN n        IS A `Notice of increase of rent`
      a        IS A `Residential tenancy agreement`
      h        IS A `Rent history`
      f        IS A `Facts for sections 99 and 100`
      holidays IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-22 reading B -- the notice` n `has effect under` a `, given` h `,` f `and the holidays` holidays IF
    IF `s 100(4) -- reaches the notice` n `under` a `, given` f
    THEN `s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
    ELSE CONSIDER `FK-22 reading B -- the version of s 30 that governs` n `under` a `, given` f
         WHEN `section 30 as in force before 29 July 2024` THEN `on` `the readings taken (s 30(1)(b))` `, former s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
         WHEN `section 30 as in force from 29 July 2024` THEN `s 30 -- the notice` n `increases the rent under` a `from the day it specifies, given` h `and the holidays` holidays
